The fifth section adds a relation type RFIG has not previously deployed: a meta-level manifests that takes other manifests relations as its object. The Buddha Triad manifests śūnyatā precisely through the simultaneity of its other manifestations — emptiness is demonstrated by the fact that no single identification exhausts the figures. This is a recursive use of the manifests relation, where what is manifested is the doctrinal status of multiple manifestations.
